    rsXx8000DvbT2RcvEventsTable OBJECT-TYPE
      SYNTAX SEQUENCE OF RsXx8000DvbT2RcvEventsEntry
      MAX-ACCESS not-accessible
      STATUS current
      DESCRIPTION
        "This table contains necessary information for handling notifications.
        For each notification you have the following information: 
        - name (get),
        - mask to enable/disable sending out (set/get),
        - priority (set/get) and 
        - the current state (get only)."
      ::= { rsXx8000DvbT2RcvEvents 1 }

    
    rsXx8000DvbT2RcvEventsEntry OBJECT-TYPE
      SYNTAX RsXx8000DvbT2RcvEventsEntry
      MAX-ACCESS not-accessible
      STATUS current
      DESCRIPTION
        "An event entry always consists of its indexes
        (used for addressing within redundancy systems) and 3 values:
        - name: an enumerated list of all possible notifications
        - mask: the corresponding mask (enable/disable)
        - priority: the corresponding priority (value in range 0..255)
        - event: the event itself (active/inactive)"
      INDEX { evtBoardIdx, evtNameIdx }
      ::= { rsXx8000DvbT2RcvEventsTable 1 }

    
    RsXx8000DvbT2RcvEventsEntry ::=
      SEQUENCE { 
        evtBoardIdx
          IndexAB,
        evtNameIdx
          EventMaxEntryNumber,
        evtName
          INTEGER,
        evtMask
          EventMask,
        evtPriority
          EventPriority,
        evtEvent
          EventState
       }

    evtBoardIdx OBJECT-TYPE
      SYNTAX IndexAB
      MAX-ACCESS not-accessible
